Answer: Even and odd numbers can be identified as follows:

```java
if (i % 2 == 0) {
System.out.println(i + " is even");
}
if (i % 2 != 0) {
System.out.println(i + " is odd");
}
```

The condition i % 2 == 0 identifies even numbers, while i % 2 != 0 identifies odd numbers.

Answer: A method can accept a number and return a Boolean value:

```java
class NumberManipulation {
boolean isPrime(int n) {
for (int i = 2; i < n; i++) {
if (n % i == 0) {
return false;
}
}
return true;
}
}
```

The method returns: true if the number is prime. false if the number is not prime.

Answer: An object of the NumberManipulation class can be created and used to call the method:

```java
